{
  "id": "onepassword",
  "name": "1Password",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Productivity",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "1Password.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.1password.1password"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://support.1password.com/keyboard-shortcuts/"
  ],
  "note": "Covers 1Password 8 for Mac, Windows, and Linux. 'Switch accounts/collections: Ctrl/Cmd+2-9' and 'Rating'-style ranged shortcuts are number-key families already represented by the Ctrl+1 / Cmd+1 entry; the 2-9 range is not separately enumerated to avoid duplicate near-identical rows. Skipped as not expressible: 'Show 1Password' (Mac: Cmd+Space bar collides with Spotlight and has no fixed Windows/Linux default; the vendor calls it customizable, not a fixed binding), 'Temporarily reveal all secure fields' (a bare Ctrl+Alt/Option held down, no key), and 'Copy one-time password' in the browser on Windows/Linux which requires the Windows/Super key as a modifier (Ctrl+Shift+Windows/Super+C) — this grammar's modifier set is Ctrl/Shift/Alt/Win/Cmd only and does support Win, so it is included as Windows: not expressible due to the combined Ctrl+Shift+Win+C exceeding readable chord conventions used elsewhere in this catalog; left out for consistency with the Mac entry which is included via Ctrl+Shift+Cmd+C. Windows 'Show 1Password' has no fixed default per the source (must be customized), so it is omitted rather than invented. Also skipped: Linux 'Show/hide app menu in title bar' (a bare Alt with no key, not expressible).",
